                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="letter-spacing:0in">For Persons Eligible for Medi-Cal</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">The Health Insurance Premium Payment (HIPP) Program may pay COBRA premiums in certain cases for persons eligible for Medi-Cal. You may e-mail your questions to the Department of Health Care Services at: www.HIPP@dhs.ca.gov.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">For Persons Disabled by HIV/AIDS</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">Under the Comprehensive AIDS Resources Emergency (CARE) Act of 1990, the Health Insurance Premium Payment (HIPP) Program may pay COBRA premiums for persons unable to work because of a disability due to HIV/AIDS. You may e-mail your questions to the Department of Health Care Services at: www.HIPP@dhs.ca.gov.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-weight:bold;text-decoration:underline;letter-spacing:0in">Keep your plan informed of address changes</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">In order to protect your and your family's rights, you should keep the CSUF - Human Resources and applicable dental and vision carriers/COBRA administrators informed of any changes in your address and the addresses of family members. You should also keep a copy, for your records, of any notices you send to these entities.</p></body>
